# Third-party licenses

Cerulion's binaries statically link their dependency graph, so this archive
redistributes the crates listed below. Most of their licenses require the
license text and the copyright notice to accompany a binary distribution, and
this file is that record: each crate grouped under the license it is used
under, with the full text of that license below it.

It is generated by `cargo about` from the locked dependency graph, resolved
for the union of the four released platforms, so it is the same file in every
archive. The scope is the whole Cerulion workspace rather than one binary's
tree, which makes it a superset: a crate reached only by a component this
archive does not carry is still listed. That is deliberate. A surplus
attribution costs a reader nothing, while a missing one is the failure this
file exists to prevent.

Crates that are not published are excluded, which is the test fixtures and the
internal crates that ship in nothing. Cerulion's own published crates do
appear, under AGPL-3.0-only, since they are part of what the binaries link;
the AGPL-3.0-only text itself is in the `LICENSE` file beside this one.
`NOTICE` carries the hand-written attributions, and `LICENSE-BSD-3-CLAUSE` the
BSD text the vendored ROS 2 message packages require.

The policy this is generated under, including the accepted license list and
the per-crate exceptions, is `tools/release/about.toml`. Its accepted
list mirrors the `[licenses]` allow list in `deny.toml`, so this inventory
cannot contain a license the project's own dependency audit would refuse.

